{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1509 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d78e0031eaec75beb2f278f4e83b1462d86013a048a5e5fb6ef9c36c1162054b" :edb/db-before-t 1508 :edb/db-after-t 1509 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534821 50 #inst "2026-10-12T16:32:01.978Z" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186124254 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- $f_x(x,y)=x+2y$ and $f_y(x,y)=2y-x$\n\n- $f_x(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$ and $f_y(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$\n\n- $f_x(x,y)=-\\sin{x}\\sin{y}$ and $f_y(x,y)=\\cos{x}\\cos{y}$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 false] [17592186124254 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $f_x(x,y)=x+2y$ and $f_y(x,y)=2y-x$\n\nII. $f_x(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$ and $f_y(x,y)=5(x+y)^4$\n\nIII. $f_x(x,y)=-\\sin{x}\\sin{y}$ and $f_y(x,y)=\\cos{x}\\cos{y}$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186124448 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437089 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186124448 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437090 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186124449 1038 #edb/ref 17592186437088 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186124742 1050 960.0 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186125729 1064 "Suppose that $f(x,y) = x y^2 - x^3 y.$ Then the first-order partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} (x,y) = y^2 -3x^2y \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x,y) = 2xy -x^3,\n$$\n\nand the second-order **mixed partial derivatives** are \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}(x,y) = 2y -3x^2 \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad  \\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}(x,y) = 2y-3x^2.\n$$\n\nNotice that these two mixed partial derivatives are equal, i.e., \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}=\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}.\n$$\n\nIn general, if a function $f(x,y)$ has continuous first-order partial derivatives on an open set $U,$ and the second-order mixed partial derivatives exist and are continuous on $U,$ then the mixed partial derivatives are equal everywhere on $U.$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186125729 1064 "Suppose that $f(x,y) = x y^2 - x^3 y.$ Then the first-order partial derivatives are $$\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x} (x,y) = y^2 -3x^2y \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}(x,y) = 2xy -x^3,$$\n\nand the second-order **mixed partial derivatives** are $$\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}(x,y) = 2y -3x^2 \\quad \\mathrm{and} \\quad \\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}(x,y) = 2y-3x^2.$$\n\nNotice that these two mixed partial derivatives are equal, i.e., $$\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial y\\, \\partial x}=\\dfrac{\\partial^2 f}{\\partial x\\, \\partial y}.$$\n\nIn general, if a function $f(x,y)$ has continuous first-order partial derivatives on an open set $U,$ and the second-order mixed partial derivatives exist and are continuous on $U,$ then the mixed partial derivatives are equal everywhere on $U.$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 false] [17592186268926 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{e}^{3x+2y}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{e}^{3x+2y}+6xy$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=4{y}^{2}-15{x}^{2}y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=8xy-5{x}^{3}$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6x{y}^{3}$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 false] [17592186268926 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=3{e}^{3x+2y}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{e}^{3x+2y}+6xy$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=4{y}^{2}-15{x}^{2}y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=8xy-5{x}^{3}$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6x{y}^{3}$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186383342 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 false] [17592186383342 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2y{e}^{2x-{y}^{2}}$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-{y}^{2})$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437070 1080 "a=3,\\,b=\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437070 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437070 1083 #uuid "090cb572-cfdb-5f1c-ab62-85230fae9ba1" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437071 1080 "a=3,\\,b=2" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437071 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437071 1083 #uuid "17ff528c-3c19-55ef-aada-a825dbe38568" 13194139534821 17592186045417 true] [17592186437072 1080 "a=2,\\,b=3" 13194139534821 1759218604